From: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: sc23xx: finish the scan when the interface goes down

Taking wlan0 down while a scan is outstanding trips two cfg80211 WARNs in a
row, both from the same orphaned request:

  WARNING: net/wireless/core.c:1703 cfg80211_netdev_notifier_call+0x3f4/0x45c
   __dev_notify_flags / netif_change_flags / do_setlink / rtnl_newlink
	(NetworkManager bringing the interface down)

  WARNING: net/wireless/scan.c:1192 cfg80211_scan_done+0x5c/0xd8
   sc23xx_notify_scan_done+0x4c/0x88 [sc23xx_wlan]
   sc23xx_handle_event+0x784/0xad0 [sc23xx_wlan]

sc23xx_close() flushes the event workqueue and closes the vif but never
retires vif->scan_req, so cfg80211 reaches NETDEV_DOWN with rdev->scan_req
still un-notified and warns before force-completing it itself. The firmware's
scan-done event then arrives on the event kworker and hands that same, now
stale, request back through cfg80211_scan_done() - the second WARN, on a
request cfg80211 has already finished with.

Complete the scan from ndo_stop instead. sc23xx_notify_scan_done() already
takes scan_lock and clears vif->scan_req, and cfg80211_scan_done() only
stamps the request and queues rdev->scan_done_wk, so it is safe here; running
it before NETDEV_DOWN sets ->notified and both WARNs go away.

While here, fix the error path in sc23xx_scan(). Once vif->scan_req has been
published the mutex is already dropped, so the "goto err_out" taken when
sc23xx_cmd_set_probe_req_ie() fails unlocks scan_lock a second time and
leaves vif->scan_req pointing at a request cfg80211 frees as soon as ->scan()
returns an error - the same stale pointer the WARNs above are about, reached
by a different route. Split the two failure cases apart.

Signed-off-by: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/unisoc/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/unisoc/main.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/unisoc/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/unisoc/main.c
@@ -141,8 +141,8 @@ static int sc23xx_scan(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct cfg80211_scan_request *reques
 
 	mutex_lock(&vif->scan_lock);
 	if (vif->scan_req) {
-		ret = -EBUSY;
-		goto err_out;
+		mutex_unlock(&vif->scan_lock);
+		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
 	vif->scan_req = request;
@@ -152,18 +152,23 @@ static int sc23xx_scan(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct cfg80211_scan_request *reques
 		ret = sc23xx_cmd_set_probe_req_ie(vif, request->ie,
 						  request->ie_len);
 		if (ret)
-			goto err_out;
+			goto err_drop;
 	}
 
 	ret = sc23xx_cmd_scan(vif, request);
-	if (ret) {
-		sc23xx_notify_scan_done(vif, true);
-		return ret;
-	}
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_drop;
 
 	return 0;
 
-err_out:
+err_drop:
+	/*
+	 * cfg80211 owns the request again the moment ->scan() returns an
+	 * error, so drop our pointer rather than handing it back later
+	 * through cfg80211_scan_done().
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&vif->scan_lock);
+	vif->scan_req = NULL;
 	mutex_unlock(&vif->scan_lock);
 	return ret;
 }
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/unisoc/vif.c b/drivers/net/wireless/unisoc/vif.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/unisoc/vif.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/unisoc/vif.c
@@ -90,6 +90,12 @@ static int sc23xx_close(struct net_device *ndev)
 	struct sc23xx_vif *vif = netdev_priv(ndev);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Retire any outstanding scan before cfg80211 gets NETDEV_DOWN and
+	 * finds rdev->scan_req un-notified (WARN in core.c), and before the
+	 * firmware's scan-done event can hand the stale request back.
+	 */
+	sc23xx_notify_scan_done(vif, true);
 	flush_workqueue(vif->sdev->evt_wq);
 
 	ret = sc23xx_cmd_close(vif);
